meta {
  name: Create Asset
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/assets
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "url": "https://picsum.photos/id/237/300/300.jpg",
    "filename": "wc_test_asset.jpg",
    "alt_text": "WC test asset",
    "category_ids": ["6a9f1b862b6fd055ffb7c7de"]
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
  res.body.data.content_type: eq image/jpeg
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-08 against "David's Dev Account". **Fixture
  kept** -- id `6aa021b72b6fd055ffb7ca9f`, for Products (Phase 2b)'s
  `thumbnail_id`.

  `201 Created`. Plytix downloaded the public image from `url` and stored
  it (`content_type`, `checksum`, `extension`, `file_size` all populated
  from the real file).

  ## Major finding -- category_ids is silently ignored on create
  `category_ids` was sent with a real category id (Phase 1b's fixture)
  but **does not link** -- a follow-up `GET /assets/{id}/categories`
  right after this create returns `[]`. The linkage only takes effect via
  a separate `PATCH` after creation -- see "Update Asset.bru" in this
  folder, which sets `category_ids` again and confirms it actually
  applies that time. **This is resource-specific**: the same
  `category_ids` field on `POST /products` (Phase 2b) *does* link at
  create time -- don't assume this behavior generalizes across resources
  either way; test per-resource.
}
